      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "You cannot view detailed shader properties at runtime, including keyword count or keyword name-- at least, in a useful manner. You have to load the shader in the first place, as far as I understand, which would kind of invalidate this system. This is an engine (as in, Unity) limitation.\n\nBlacklisting has similar problems, as it is trivial to change a shader to get around any kind of blacklist (change the name by one letter, for instance).\n\nWe recognize the root issues, however, and continue to investigate ways to reduce these problems.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
