  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-04-10T16:23:03.773Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Performance Option Toggle for a Shader Blacklist Limiter that blocks shaders by Keywords via an expandable custom list similar to the particle and dynamic bone limiter. \n\nThe longer the game has been out the more things have been developed for it. Shaders being one of these things. Sadly due to human nature some of these shaders are much more malicious than others. Some examples would be zoom shaders, screenspace shaders, and shaders that completely remove ones ability to do anything unless you enter safety mode. Sure we have safety settings, but once you are friends you sadly will see them unless that users avatar is hidden. Recently a terrible video emerged of someone using such a shader to purposely trigger seizures to a user on their friend list. It isn't a permanent solution but long term might be a good idea to add another performance option to VRChat that lets a user toggle on a Blacklist for common malicious shaders that can be expanded on. There are obviously ways around it but the majority of people with these shaders won't know how to get around them and/or all avatars currently circulating with them would become useless unless updated. In order for the community to create a robust blacklist over time we may eventually need a way to view what assets or shaders are in an avatar on some kind of advanced tab.",
